        "id": "a-round-keeps-a-candidate-on-development-cases-and-recommends-one-on-held-out-cases",
        "statement": "A candidate of a round is kept when, on a development test case, it has the best rate among the candidates and beats the source version's rate there; the round recommends the kept candidate with the highest mean on the held-out cases among those at least likely improved, and recommends none while it has fewer standings than candidates or while any built candidate's batch is not settled.",
        "contexts": [
          "eval"
        ],
        "examples": [
          "Two candidates tied at the best development rate above the source are both kept; one equal to the source is not.",
          "While one candidate's batch is still running no candidate is recommended, even if another is likely improved.",
          "An unavailable candidate with no batch does not hold the recommendation back."
        ],
